Btrfs(B-tree File System)

	File System		Best Use Case
	ext4			Default, stable, widely used
	Btrfs			Snapshots, rollback, SSDs
	XFS			Servers, logs, large files
	ZFS			Data integrity, RAID, NAS (ZFSonLinux)
	F2FS			Phones, SSDs, flash storage
	bcachefs (new)		Hybrid of Btrfs + ZFS ideas (in testing)

Notes
    ext4 is still the most common default FS in many distros (Ubuntu, Debian).
    Btrfs is used by Manjaro, openSUSE (default), Fedora (optional).
    XFS is default in RHEL/CentOS.
    ZFS is great for data reliability, used in NAS (e.g., FreeNAS/TrueNAS), but not included in Linux kernel due to licensing (CDDL vs GPL).
    F2FS is common in Android phones.


